{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"929377169382ef94fc9269f7b427e160a7f1389beabc8063e166afe4fd74a0d3","digest":{"component_or_area":"Bedrock LLM provider","key_entities":["REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","build_bedrock_provider","BedrockProvider","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","review-bot service","LLMConfigError","boto3.session.Session().region_name"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","region","configuration","cutover","review-bot","llm"],"propositions":["The review-bot container lacks explicit AWS region configuration, causing boto3 to fail with NoRegionError during BedrockProvider construction.","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION and AWS_DEFAULT_REGION are required separately — the rebar config knob does not automatically populate boto3's region resolution.","build_bedrock_provider must pre-check boto3 region resolution and raise a typed LLMConfigError naming the rebar setting, not rely on catching pydantic-ai UserError.","IMDS reachability does not supply region information to boto3; region configuration is independent of IMDS hop-limit contingencies.","Review-bot CloudWatch voter metrics fail silently for the same missing-region reason, impacting eb6e's rollback alarm."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787714022093570001,"uuid":"63228cf7-2d26-44d8-a37c-47303904ce41"}